body:
The `AGENTS.md`-hygiene surface of the distributed agent-builder template `opencode-suite/agents/agent-builder.md` (product source embedded via `include_str!` and installed by `apg init` into `~/.opencode/agents/`). It carries:
- the `AGENTS.md` write grant: the template's `permissions` array (`{ action: edit, resource: ""*"", effect: deny }` with the allow entries under it) allows the repo-root `AGENTS.md` ALONGSIDE `.opencode/agents/**` and `opencode.json`, resolved against the session workspace root (the main checkout), mirrored nowhere under `apg/.worktrees/*/` and broadened nowhere beyond those paths — so the hygiene instruction is executable;
- the hygiene rules: `AGENTS.md` aligns with the distributed-agent rules and carries nothing about the canonical change-set flow (owned solely and immutably by `codebase-navigator`, `requirements.requirement.navigator-staged-flow`) — the agent-builder AUDITS for consistency and REMOVES any flow content; it adds nothing about the navigator and restates the flow nowhere;
- the NON-DESTRUCTIVE merge rule (all repo-specific content — build gates, test tiers, pipeline, release steps — preserved);
- the only-when-present rule (`AGENTS.md` is optional per project; the agent-builder manufactures one only where a project carries one);
- the universality statement (every apg project; the apg repo's local `build-implementer` also touching `AGENTS.md` is a local arrangement rather than a universal rule).

It is distinct from `solution.component.agent-builder-prompt`, which owns the same file's broad surface enumeration, while this component owns the `AGENTS.md`-hygiene surface; `rust.apg.plan_cmd.verify.coverage_check` maps this requirement's coverage to the single edited file `opencode-suite/agents/agent-builder.md`, the component's only `implemented-by` target. Product source in `solution.container.opencode-suite`; the repo's own `.opencode/agents/**` and `AGENTS.md` are consumer artifacts.
